<title>USA: CME April volume rises 28.4 pct year-on-year.</title>
<headline>CME April volume rises 28.4 pct year-on-year.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange said its futures and options volume totaled 19,187,380 contracts in April, up 28.4 percent from 14,945,036 contracts a year earlier.</p>
<p>Open interest at the end of the month stood at 6,896,009 contracts, up 12.0 percent from 6,158,435 at the end of April last year.</p>
<p>Year-to-date volume through April totaled 72,777,942 contracts, up 5.6 percent from 68,926,128 during the same period in 1996.  </p>
<p>Major categories and volumes were as follows:</p>
<p>Futures (individual)  April 1997    % change	 April 1996</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	    10,171,059	 +33.8	  7,600,477</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	     516,852	 + 0.5	    514,419</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	     402,703	 - 6.5	    430,601</p>
<p>  Swiss franc		343,582	 + 6.1	    323,876</p>
<p>  British pound	    185,273	 -39.6	    306,759</p>
<p>  Canadian dollar	     151,141	 +14.7	    131,813</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  1,804,159	 +32.5	  1,361,167</p>
<p>  Live cattle		335,771	 -27.2	    461,349</p>
<p>  Live/lean hogs	   215,986	 - 1.5	    219,378</p>
<p>Options on futures</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   2,084,483	  +35.3	   1,540,301</p>
<p>  Eurodollar midcurve     815,493	 +287.0	     210,722</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   130,521	  -33.7	     196,861</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   140,347	  -26.7	     191,532</p>
<p>  British pound	  156,041	  -40.5	     262,155</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  544,756	  +40.0	     389,224</p>
<p>  Live cattle	     80,498	  - 2.1		82,224</p>
<p>  Live/lean hogs	  30,538	  +30.7		23,369</p>
<p>Since January 1994 CME has counted in volume anything that creates or liquidates open positions including expired options and SIMEX mutual offset transactions cleared on the CME.</p>
<p>Excluding these transactions, CME &quot;pit traded&quot; volume for April 1997 totaled 17,629,985 and year-to-date volume totaled 65,848,606.</p>
